                <name>Extreme Heat — Persian Gulf</name>
                <Placemark id="250">
                    <name>Extreme Heat — Persian Gulf</name>
                    <description>Persian Gulf extreme heat zone — wet-bulb temperatures exceed human survivability threshold (35°C) for brief annual periods. Summer temperatures routinely exceed 50°C in Iraq, Kuwait, Saudi Arabia, and Iran. APPROXIMATE — Narrative-derived polygon. Replace with data-driven geometry when source dataset becomes available. See: 2050-snapshot/domains/climate.md#west-asia--middle-east</description>
